      "text": "/skill:tidy-recipe-authoring\n\nCreate tidy recipes for workbook `5dbd0ac29918698496cae3946ba62b1a4a9b5048501806013b5aabbc0a127f0d--recorded-crime-offenders-2021-22-cube-4-source.xlsx`.\n\n- Publication: Recorded Crime — Offenders (Australian Bureau of Statistics)\n- Release or year: 2021\n- Sheets needing a recipe: 5 of 5\n\n| sheet | sheet_sha256 | current recipe |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Contents\" | 1ffaf4d84b8ea2190df603ae701526f9617565f4ec220d3e42ce9f85d6c9e394 | missing |\n| \"Table 23\" | aa4499509c81578326a0d596f9d9fcbd31c7c62d78c5ed95f71bc0053de60479 | missing |\n| \"Table 24\" | fc38ecb31b0b6a820dafcf55efc2c20148ccd3b127cc71965941ec76d33decaf | missing |\n| \"Table 25\" | e760510fe16a77aad4cf6d729801431419f6f26f68704043204f806f5d32915d | missing |\n| \"Table 26\" | b43e64f921da26cf558414a2f098bbc3f6fde3eb6cec354f80ccd7fe50ad518d | missing |\n\nRelated workbooks:\n- None\n\nWork through every sheet listed above using the skill's workflow. Use\n`codemode` scripts to call the recipe tools, and batch the work: for example,\nlist the workbook and check templates for all sheets in one script, then read\ngrids and test recipes a few sheets at a time. Keep script output short.\n\nName dimensions from `dictionary/dimensions.csv` (see the skill's\n`references/naming.md`); declare any name it lacks in `new_dimensions`.\n\nWrite each recipe to `tidy-recipes/<sheet_sha256>.json` and finish every sheet\nwith `submit_recipe`. You may only write recipe files for this workbook.\n\nEnd with one line per sheet: `sheet | kind | status | records | remaining failures`."
